WEBVTT

00:41.791 --> 00:46.004
MY ROYAL NEMESIS

00:49.758 --> 00:53.261
Do you all remember the Star of the
Temptress? The comet that appeared

00:53.344 --> 00:56.931
alongside the total solar eclipse three
months ago can still be seen in the

00:57.015 --> 01:00.810
night sky. We will all feel a sense
of loss when it suddenly disappears.

01:00.894 --> 01:04.647
So I recommend taking a photo of it now
while you still can. Unlike meteors

01:04.731 --> 01:08.443
and shooting stars, that vanish in the
blink of an eye, this star appeared

01:08.526 --> 01:15.450
silently and can disappear
without warning at any moment.

01:22.874 --> 01:26.127
EPISODE 10
HOPE, DESPAIR, AND LONGING

01:36.304 --> 01:40.225
Oh, I'm so sorry, but the chairman is
sleeping. I understand, I just can't let

01:40.308 --> 01:44.270
you in right now. But I'll be sure to let
him know you stopped by when he wakes

01:44.354 --> 01:45.855
up. Goodbye.

02:07.418 --> 02:12.924
So I'm the, uh… Grand Prince that
was exiled and you're the court lady?

02:13.007 --> 02:14.050
That's right.

02:15.844 --> 02:20.515
The dreams mean something after all.
I'm seeing visions of our past lives.

02:22.600 --> 02:23.601
You are.

02:24.894 --> 02:28.606
So what's your deal? Are you in
a time slip or something?

02:31.526 --> 02:36.781
Uh… not at all. My spirit traversed
through the ages.

02:39.367 --> 02:40.493
That's the same thing.

02:41.536 --> 02:43.538
No wonder you sound so old-fashioned.

02:44.831 --> 02:48.293
But this isn't some X-Files episode.
How is this possible?

02:49.460 --> 02:50.712
You said you believed me.

02:51.254 --> 02:54.757
I know, I know. I'm just struggling to
make sense of it, but given the

02:54.841 --> 02:56.092
situation…

02:59.888 --> 03:00.722
I'll do my best.

03:02.056 --> 03:03.600
Would you go see a doctor?

03:03.683 --> 03:04.642
A doctor?

03:06.436 --> 03:10.023
I just mean, it is possible that… we've
completely lost our minds. Some

03:10.106 --> 03:14.027
professional tests would be… an
awful idea.

03:20.950 --> 03:22.160
Does this mean that our…

03:24.287 --> 03:25.622
trial period is done with?

03:26.539 --> 03:28.499
Why ask me that? You're embarrassing me

03:29.000 --> 03:32.837
Well, you know, I just wanted to make
sure I wasn't getting ahead of myself.

03:35.089 --> 03:38.551
We have smashed our lips together enough,
I suppose the trial period no

03:38.635 --> 03:40.553
longer makes sense.

03:45.225 --> 03:50.688
No. So it means we're on day one
from today, right?

03:56.861 --> 03:59.072
Promise me one thing. From now on,
there are--

03:59.155 --> 04:00.740
No secrets between us ever.

04:01.616 --> 04:05.245
Yeah, exactly. And if Choi Mun-do
shows up for--

04:05.328 --> 04:07.330
I'll tell you immediately if he does.

04:08.122 --> 04:11.626
That's right. I'm the jealous type,
understand? And I don't mean just him,

04:11.709 --> 04:15.213
I don't want you to be involved with,
or to talk to, or to meet any guys.

04:15.296 --> 04:18.341
Hey, how am I supposed to work then?
Half the world is male. Am I meant to

04:18.424 --> 04:21.928
shut myself off from the world?

04:22.428 --> 04:24.222
Well, I'm just making a point.

04:26.641 --> 04:27.809
Anyway, given all that…

04:30.853 --> 04:34.565
how about we go inside to finish our
conversation?

04:40.280 --> 04:44.242
Ugh, for God's sake. Who left this here,
huh?

04:45.243 --> 04:46.494
H-how long have you been there?

04:46.577 --> 04:50.456
Oh, I just came up to water the
plants and missed my chance to leave.

04:51.499 --> 04:53.251
Don't worry, do carry on.

04:53.334 --> 04:55.086
Why is he being so nice?

04:55.169 --> 04:58.298
I can water the plants tomorrow. But you
can't stay overnight.

04:59.507 --> 05:01.342
Manager fellow! Such impropriety.

05:02.385 --> 05:03.219
I can't?

05:06.014 --> 05:06.848
Of course not.

05:12.395 --> 05:16.190
You're right. That's a step too far
for a Joseon woman, I guess.

05:19.027 --> 05:22.488
No, I'm no longer a Joseon woman.
From now on, I won't be stingy with

05:22.572 --> 05:26.659
my heart, or suffer in silence.
I'll open up and give freely.

05:37.503 --> 05:38.338
Give me more.

05:39.505 --> 05:41.382
GIFTING HEALTH THROUGH CARE
AFFECTION

05:42.258 --> 05:45.553
Heat in a double boiler and take it
after breakfast and dinner.

05:45.636 --> 05:48.389
How many times have I told her
this is all marketing?

05:48.473 --> 05:52.018
Quit the smartass comments about
marketing and don't miss a single dose.

05:52.101 --> 05:55.980
What the hell? Is she a mind-reader?

05:56.064 --> 05:59.484
Consider it my way of showing how much I
cherish you. Signing off.

06:00.777 --> 06:01.611
Cherish?

06:06.199 --> 06:07.658
I'll do it just for you.

06:18.294 --> 06:19.128
Just took it.

06:21.798 --> 06:25.593
I'm going to give freely from now on.
Not only my heart, but I will spend all

06:25.676 --> 06:27.720
my money openly.

06:28.221 --> 06:29.055
That's my girl.

06:30.014 --> 06:30.848
Here.

06:32.850 --> 06:36.604
Grandma, whatever you want. Just
let me know, okay? You want any clothes?

06:36.687 --> 06:40.066
Buy yourself some first. Ugh, what
a waste of your beauty.

06:40.650 --> 06:44.570
Oh, yeah. It is a waste. Time goes by
and you can never get it back. I'm going

06:44.654 --> 06:47.615
to live without regrets.

06:51.828 --> 06:55.498
I'll live life to the fullest. I'll be
generous and give openly. That's what

06:55.581 --> 06:57.458
it means to live a good life.

07:02.964 --> 07:05.925
This is really sweet. They said
these apples got snowed on, but they

07:06.008 --> 07:06.843
taste great!

07:08.386 --> 07:10.263
Oh, my little angel.

07:18.521 --> 07:21.983
That's right. Leave apples too long
and they rot. All things spoil if

07:22.066 --> 07:24.902
hoarded. Here, take it.

07:27.738 --> 07:28.781
Why are you giving us these?

07:28.865 --> 07:31.951
Well, I bought them all because they were
on sale. They said they were snowed on,

07:32.034 --> 07:33.786
but they're actually sweet.

07:38.458 --> 07:40.710
What's going on? Maybe they've
been poisoned.

07:40.793 --> 07:41.627
Hilarious.

07:42.295 --> 07:43.129
Manager fellow!

07:44.130 --> 07:45.423
Jesus, you scared me

07:45.506 --> 07:49.135
Here. You got me my place, you take my
deliveries. I've always wanted to

07:49.218 --> 07:52.555
thank you for everything. There's no
manager fellow quite like you

07:52.638 --> 07:55.892
in the world. Let us stay this way
forever.

07:58.853 --> 08:01.856
My Gwang-nam, I was wondering where you
were. And here you are.

08:01.939 --> 08:02.773
"My Gwang-nam?"

08:03.399 --> 08:06.027
Here, I want you to try this. It's very
sweet.

08:06.110 --> 08:07.862
You really want me to have this? For
free?

08:07.945 --> 08:10.490
Of course it's free. Why would I
charge you for an apple? You think

08:10.573 --> 08:11.491
so little of me?

08:11.574 --> 08:14.118
Why are you suddenly being so generous?
That's not like you.

08:14.202 --> 08:18.456
Why is that an issue? What do you mean,
it's not like me? I look pure as snow.

08:18.998 --> 08:21.125
As long as I stay silent and do not
speak.

08:22.376 --> 08:23.669
Who on earth told you that?

08:23.753 --> 08:24.754
The fruit seller woman.

08:24.837 --> 08:27.840
Let me guess, she also said you have a
sparking personality?

08:28.591 --> 08:32.136
Can you believe this? Look, they're all
completely frozen at the bottom.

08:32.220 --> 08:33.387
What? Frozen?

08:34.972 --> 08:38.392
That's terrible. In my town, we wouldn't
harvest ones like that.

08:38.976 --> 08:41.646
Oh, no. I sent them to someone already.

08:41.729 --> 08:43.272
CHA SE-GYE

08:43.356 --> 08:47.944
Mr. Son. Who on earth would send apples
to Mr. Cha?

08:49.028 --> 08:52.782
A crate of apples is well known to mean
conspiracy, corruption, and acts of

08:52.865 --> 08:56.786
collusion between politics and business.

09:00.206 --> 09:01.040
You're looking inside?

09:01.123 --> 09:02.583
Ms. Kim, you should watch out.

09:02.667 --> 09:04.293
A bomb could be in there.

09:04.377 --> 09:07.046
I think perhaps we should call
for back up instead.

09:07.129 --> 09:10.841
Don't worry. I served in the Marines.
First Division,

09:13.678 --> 09:14.637
A Poison Frog.

09:20.601 --> 09:23.688
-I'd leave that alone if I were you.
-Mr. Cha, please stay back.

09:23.771 --> 09:26.190
Don't touch it. It's mine, Son.

09:40.246 --> 09:44.667
I'm sure it is. It's Shin Seo-ri's.
It's the second gift she's sent to me.

09:45.209 --> 09:48.129
The second? What was the first one?

09:48.212 --> 09:49.046
Uh, she…

09:49.547 --> 09:53.092
got me some herbal medicine. It seems
that she cherishes me. Something

09:53.175 --> 09:56.887
like that. You know, when you, uh, care
about someone you worry about them

09:56.971 --> 09:58.222
and stuff.

10:03.644 --> 10:06.063
It's more concern than affection,
if you ask me.

10:09.400 --> 10:10.234
Concern?

10:10.318 --> 10:13.195
About your well being. Especially your…
stamina. I think that's what she's

10:13.279 --> 10:14.113
concerned about.

10:24.415 --> 10:25.249
Stamina?

10:25.333 --> 10:28.377
But even more importantly, I have an
update about the nurse.

10:29.962 --> 10:32.381
Oh, tell me. What's going on with her?

10:32.465 --> 10:35.551
She'll turn herself in once this is over.
Until then, she's under our protection,

10:35.635 --> 10:36.469
sir.

10:36.552 --> 10:41.766
Yeah? Let's avoid unnecessary bloodshed.
Be as discreet as possible.

10:42.433 --> 10:45.895
That's all well and good, sir, but
the regime is about to change.

10:47.229 --> 10:48.064
Regime?

10:51.317 --> 10:54.737
Sir, please forgive me. I was wrong.

10:55.363 --> 10:59.325
Forgive you for what? Did I punish you
for anything?

11:00.326 --> 11:04.246
Please give me one more chance. You know
how hard I've worked for the firm all

11:04.330 --> 11:05.581
this time.

11:06.957 --> 11:10.503
Well now, Mun-do, the problem is no
salaried employee works that hard for

11:10.586 --> 11:14.799
their firm, understand? You were happy to
give so much because you thought it was

11:14.882 --> 11:18.928
yours. Oh, dear. I've worked you for too
long, I suppose. It's high time you took

11:19.011 --> 11:23.015
things a little easier. Go to the U.S.
It'll be an opportunity for you to spend

11:23.099 --> 11:30.064
some time with Seo-jun as his dad, before
you come back.

11:36.696 --> 11:39.490
Grandfather's ruthless. Who'd have
thought he'd bleed Mun-do dry and ship

11:39.573 --> 11:41.075
him off to the U.S.?

11:41.158 --> 11:42.326
Oh, you knew already?

11:44.245 --> 11:47.623
Do you think I was oblivious just
because I was dating? It's my job

11:47.707 --> 11:49.250
to find out about this.

11:51.502 --> 11:54.505
It's time you start to prepare yourself.
Since you're already in the

11:54.588 --> 11:57.675
know, I might as well tell you. The
chairman has been working with his

11:57.758 --> 11:59.593
attorney to have his will notarized.

12:01.554 --> 12:05.433
Oof, he's intending to just straight up
leave it all to me in this day and age?

12:05.516 --> 12:08.936
Let's just hold a beat for now.

12:13.065 --> 12:16.777
Wrap up your launch and come back to
the firm with your pride intact. You've

12:16.861 --> 12:19.864
succeeded enough to be proud of what
you've achieved.

12:20.740 --> 12:25.161
Understood, grandfather. But I have
one condition.

12:25.828 --> 12:26.662
A condition?

12:26.746 --> 12:29.582
I'm calling off my engagement with
Mochang.

12:29.665 --> 12:30.583
What?

12:30.666 --> 12:32.126
I know that I worry you.

12:32.209 --> 12:35.796
But I can stand on my own two feet,
you know that. I'm breaking it off.

12:35.880 --> 12:39.717
What did I do in my past life to deserve
this? Why are both my nephew and

12:39.800 --> 12:41.594
grandson this way?

12:42.636 --> 12:44.680
Have you told your grandfather
about the bug?

12:44.764 --> 12:46.891
What's the point? It'll just make him
worry.

12:46.974 --> 12:50.102
You should still tell him. You never
know what Mun-do might do next.

12:50.186 --> 12:52.396
I'm still nervous.

12:53.481 --> 12:56.776
If you're nervous, imagine how he'd feel.
He's relied on him for so long.

12:56.859 --> 13:00.154
Once Choi Mun-do leaves I won't have to
worry about him anymore. So until

13:00.237 --> 13:02.990
then, I need to make sure grandfather
doesn't find out.

13:04.825 --> 13:06.702
You believe he'll go without a fight?

13:09.497 --> 13:11.791
This is where the cosmic energy lies?

13:11.874 --> 13:14.585
Be quiet. This place is well-known
among insiders for the most accurate

13:14.668 --> 13:15.795
readings.

13:18.172 --> 13:20.966
Gosh. Well, um, could I get you anything
for you to drink? It's not much,

13:21.050 --> 13:23.844
but I'll whip up some coffee with these
instant coffee sticks. Excuse me.

13:23.928 --> 13:25.679
-I'll be right back.
-Ah, no…

13:27.681 --> 13:28.516
Yes.

13:32.186 --> 13:34.647
What was I thinking letting you
drag us here together. When will

13:34.730 --> 13:36.106
you come to your senses?

13:36.190 --> 13:39.109
Ju-mi, just think about it. Does Father
even listen to anything we say?

13:39.193 --> 13:41.654
Does that jerk Cha Se-gye pay
any attention to us ever? Mun-do is

13:41.737 --> 13:44.490
about to be frozen out, and you and
I have no power to do anything about

13:44.573 --> 13:51.497
it at all. All we can do is let the holy
cosmic energy guide us.

13:52.581 --> 13:56.544
I just don't get why we have to come to
a place like this to be guided?

13:57.628 --> 14:01.340
So what do you suggest we do? I told
you, our lifeline is surely out there

14:01.423 --> 14:06.554
somewhere. We're in the middle of enemy
grounds.

14:07.888 --> 14:11.100
Cha Se-gye is this. He's the door handle
to power.

14:11.183 --> 14:12.351
You think so?

14:12.434 --> 14:15.354
Too bad. My place doesn't have a door
handle. Huh? You dare infiltrate my

14:15.437 --> 14:21.235
place, you spies? Be gone, you demons.
Be gone! Out! Out!

14:21.318 --> 14:22.236
Ew, ew. Oh, my God.

14:22.319 --> 14:25.155
Out of here. Oh, the ancestors are angry,
yeah! The ancestral spirits are

14:25.239 --> 14:27.366
so angry. You've enraged them! How dare
you offend them?

14:27.449 --> 14:28.409
Oh, my God, what is this?

14:28.492 --> 14:32.621
We're leaving, we're leaving! Stop that!

14:33.831 --> 14:39.086
Be gone, leeches! Go, you vermin!
Mongrels!

14:41.297 --> 14:44.425
Why did you have to get these
rotten apples. Yuck.

14:44.508 --> 14:47.595
How could they charge me for these?
If I ever catch them, I'll make them pay

14:47.678 --> 14:48.512
for this.

14:48.596 --> 14:50.848
Why do I have to be punished with
hard labor? Business and

14:50.931 --> 14:52.892
personal matters are separate, you know?

14:52.975 --> 14:56.979
Do you not possess a conscience? Are you
trying to get paid even more money?

14:57.062 --> 14:59.982
Wow, a second ago it was, "my Gwang-nam."
You turn with the wind. What's all

15:00.065 --> 15:04.194
this anyway? Did Mr. Cha tell you he
likes nice girls?

15:04.278 --> 15:05.696
No, it's just that…

15:07.615 --> 15:09.992
Wait, what? Don't tell me you're…

15:11.118 --> 15:13.662
Come on, it was easy to guess
with that car showing up here all the

15:13.746 --> 15:16.165
time. I have eyes it's not hard to
notice.

15:16.248 --> 15:17.416
You little devil.

15:18.584 --> 15:20.544
You were playing dumb all this time.

15:22.755 --> 15:25.341
Your Highness. It's me, Fortune Teller
Geum.

15:35.225 --> 15:37.603
It's high time you took things a little
easier.

15:38.687 --> 15:42.066
Go to the U.S. It'll be an opportunity
for you to spend some time with

15:42.149 --> 15:44.318
Seo-jun as his dad before you come back.

15:56.121 --> 15:57.164
Hey, Seo-jun.

15:57.247 --> 16:00.042
Mr. Choi, Seo-jun's had a bit of an
accident.

16:00.125 --> 16:03.128
An accident? What're you talking about?

16:03.212 --> 16:06.090
He fell during a game earlier today.
He's been to the ER. He has a ligament

16:06.173 --> 16:07.049
injury.

16:08.050 --> 16:09.343
Why are you only telling me now?

16:09.426 --> 16:12.179
Seo-jun insisted that I not tell you, so
I had to wait until he'd fallen

16:12.262 --> 16:14.139
asleep to call.

16:15.641 --> 16:16.600
I'm sorry, sir.

16:16.684 --> 16:20.646
Are you? I'm your boss, not Seo-jun,
understand. Don't bother coming to work

16:20.729 --> 16:26.235
tomorrow. Your replacement will be there
tonight, so you should be ready to leave.

16:49.174 --> 16:53.303
You believe he'll go without a fight?
You never know what Mun-do might do next.

16:53.387 --> 16:58.058
Sir, I'm worried about your safety,
Shouldn't we be keeping an eye on Mun-do?

16:59.601 --> 17:01.270
What's he gonna do? Kill me?

17:20.456 --> 17:21.290
Boo.

17:22.875 --> 17:26.462
Why did you sneak up on me like that?
You almost gave me a heart attack.

17:26.545 --> 17:29.465
You came here, why are you so surprised?
What brings you?

17:29.548 --> 17:30.674
Oh, Son brought me.

17:30.758 --> 17:33.719
No, I mean, why are you here?
Something up?

17:35.137 --> 17:38.265
Well, I want to go somewhere with you.

17:39.308 --> 17:42.811
-Go where?
-A date. Let's go on a date, Cha Se-gye.

17:44.897 --> 17:47.232
Date? You mean now?

17:53.697 --> 17:54.531
Alright.

18:00.829 --> 18:03.874
Are you serious? Your idea of a date is a
bakery tour?

18:03.957 --> 18:07.294
The ring-shaped bread is famous here.
How did everyone catch wind of it so

18:07.377 --> 18:08.212
fast?

18:16.011 --> 18:19.515
I can't believe I expected something
else. Do you think it makes sense

18:19.598 --> 18:23.685
for a man like me to waste his time
standing around for this stuff?

18:24.186 --> 18:28.190
It's romance, it's not a waste of time.
I saw online that a date is spending an

18:28.273 --> 18:32.778
enjoyable day with your beloved. Isn't it
enough for us to eat yummy food together?

18:34.446 --> 18:36.949
"Beloved," you say? You can do
that anytime. On a date, you should

18:37.032 --> 18:39.701
have fireworks, or at least a yacht
party, that sort of thing. This is

18:39.785 --> 18:42.121
just mundane stuff.

18:45.332 --> 18:48.252
I enjoy it though. That's why I like it,
because it's the mundane thing that

18:48.335 --> 18:55.092
everyone does. But it's special because
we're together.

18:59.680 --> 19:01.974
Whoa, th-that's a little on the nose.

19:03.058 --> 19:06.728
Doing the things I enjoy with the one I
like to be around. It's something

19:06.812 --> 19:09.731
I've always wanted to do. Is that a
problem?

19:12.192 --> 19:13.026
No.

19:16.196 --> 19:17.156
There's no problem.

19:21.785 --> 19:22.619
So what now?

19:24.496 --> 19:26.498
What other mundane things you wanna do?

19:43.974 --> 19:47.603
Namsan? You want to ride the cable car?
Is this seriously what you want?

19:47.686 --> 19:48.812
You sure?

19:50.939 --> 19:52.774
-We can, right?
-No reason we can't.

19:53.567 --> 19:56.904
We should! I really wanna take
the ride up. According to my notes,

19:56.987 --> 20:00.282
Namsan has been a classic dating
hot spot for a long time.

20:00.782 --> 20:01.783
Hot spot?

20:01.867 --> 20:04.912
My Lovely Sam Soon, Episode Six. The
characters smash lips here, so these are

20:04.995 --> 20:07.539
known as the Sam-soon Stairs And
that's not all. Boys Over Flowers,

20:07.623 --> 20:10.250
Episode Four. Geum Jan-di went to Gu
Jun-pyo and opened up her entire

20:10.334 --> 20:11.960
heart to him.

20:13.045 --> 20:14.296
All those shows are ancient--

20:14.379 --> 20:16.965
Of course, it's not just lovers,
High Kick Through the Roof, Episode

20:17.049 --> 20:19.593
#122. When Se-kyung got Shin-ae
a free cable car ride by saying she

20:19.676 --> 20:24.973
was 47 months old, it really moved
the hearts of the nation. And so--

20:25.057 --> 20:26.558
Okay, alright, fine, fine.

20:27.059 --> 20:30.312
I've arranged everything, so all you
have to do is follow me.

20:46.078 --> 20:47.746
-This way.
-Hello.

20:55.629 --> 20:57.130
Cha Se-gye, look at that.

21:07.266 --> 21:09.601
Whoa. We're moving!

21:19.027 --> 21:22.322
Be careful, Shin Seo-ri. You don't
want to fall off.

21:22.823 --> 21:23.907
Fall off?

21:33.500 --> 21:35.669
What is this? This is highly precarious.

21:35.752 --> 21:41.466
I'll just walk. Let's get them to let
us out. Let me out! Open the door! Hey!

21:41.550 --> 21:44.511
-Open this up! Hello?
-Hey, Shin Seo-ri. Shin Seo-ri. Hey.

21:44.594 --> 21:45.971
Stop it, you're embarrassing us.

21:46.054 --> 21:50.475
Who cares about that? We need to
save ourselves. Help us! Hey!

21:51.018 --> 21:51.893
Let go.

21:53.061 --> 21:54.855
Stop it! Jesus, I can't even make a joke.

21:54.938 --> 22:00.444
What? "Joke?" You joke about a matter of
life and death? Stupid Cha Se-gye.

22:04.823 --> 22:06.199
-Are you insane?
-I am insane!

22:06.283 --> 22:07.951
-What the heck?
-His head.

22:08.035 --> 22:09.703
-Man, how obnoxious.
-Yeah, she hit…

22:09.786 --> 22:10.620
No way.

22:10.704 --> 22:12.789
-Ugh, they're so noisy.
-Jeez, what's wrong with them?

22:12.873 --> 22:14.833
-Is it a lover's tiff?
-Wow, seriously.

22:19.421 --> 22:20.839
Why would you fight in here?

22:22.007 --> 22:23.467
Oh, Cha Se-gye, look at that.

22:29.389 --> 22:31.475
Uh, I'm here. Where are you?

22:31.975 --> 22:35.771
Hey, I really need to use the bathroom.
Can you do me a solid and park my

22:35.854 --> 22:36.688
van for me?

22:36.772 --> 22:40.400
What? I'm not your valet driver.
Why would I do that?

22:40.901 --> 22:42.319
Just shut up and park it.

22:42.402 --> 22:43.945
Look, I'm not gonna go--

22:46.615 --> 22:49.201
Ugh. Are you serious.

22:53.038 --> 22:56.625
Full-time employee, my ass. As soon as
I get my paycheck for the month,

22:56.708 --> 22:59.169
I'm outta here. The triple pay's not
worth it.

23:20.315 --> 23:24.111
Ugh, why didn't you pick up your damn
phone? I was waiting.

23:25.320 --> 23:27.322
Uh, well, I-- Uh, ex-excuse me--

23:27.406 --> 23:30.200
I don't want excuses. Just take me to
Geumsonjongga.

23:30.283 --> 23:33.453
And don't forget to order the spicy
chicken feet like last time.

23:33.537 --> 23:34.579
G-G-Geumson… jong-jonga--

23:34.663 --> 23:37.207
I'm tired, so don't talk to me
until we're there.

23:38.583 --> 23:40.544
What are you doing? Come on, let's go.

23:49.136 --> 23:52.722
Oh, Cha Se-gye, look at all these
wide open views. No wonder it's a hot

23:52.806 --> 23:56.435
spot. It's perfectly situated in terms of
feng shui.

23:57.310 --> 24:00.939
I think you're the only woman who comes
here and talks about feng shui.

24:01.022 --> 24:02.941
Oh. Oh, look! Look!

24:22.335 --> 24:25.922
Cha Se-gye, I know what this is.
These are love latches. They're tokens

24:26.006 --> 24:28.592
left by lovers vowing eternal love.

24:30.844 --> 24:32.679
So should we do it?

24:36.641 --> 24:37.476
No.

24:39.352 --> 24:43.106
Why? Let's do it. I know it's a little
childish, but we've come all the way

24:43.190 --> 24:46.860
here, so why not promise eternal love?

24:47.360 --> 24:51.114
Because they say it's for eternal
love, but these don't stay here forever.

24:51.198 --> 24:54.993
If we come back later and find that
our latch is gone, I'll be a little sad.

24:55.076 --> 24:59.080
That's why I'd rather not do it.

25:00.999 --> 25:03.585
Why do you complicate things? It's just
for fun.

25:03.668 --> 25:06.630
I'm more interested in the spyglass.
Where is it?

25:08.381 --> 25:09.216
Wait up.

25:15.805 --> 25:19.100
Calm down, heart of mine. Shut up and be
quiet, just be quiet.

25:20.268 --> 25:22.938
Fucking bastard pricks, goddamn
motherfucking whack ass bitches. These

25:23.021 --> 25:25.815
assholes are insane. I used to be the
favorite, the one everyone said was

25:25.899 --> 25:28.818
flawless, and now look at this! They're
commenting that I have dead eyes and

25:28.902 --> 25:34.491
pointing out my flaws? They're being so
mean!

25:37.244 --> 25:39.079
What kind of jerks dare to say that?

25:39.579 --> 25:42.499
The Kingdom of Women chat. Everybody's
saying I suck and that I'm a terrible

25:42.582 --> 25:45.293
actress, but do they know how difficult
it is? I'd like to see them try

25:45.377 --> 25:46.878
it! Damn it.

25:47.420 --> 25:50.465
How dare they call you terrible? Those
fucking assholes!

25:50.549 --> 25:54.678
Right? Fucking bitches! Do you have a
cold or something? Your voice is…

25:56.388 --> 25:58.139
Oh, my God! Who- who are you?

25:58.932 --> 26:00.684
Oh, uh, hi, hello, Ji-hyo. I'm Shin
Seo-ri's--

26:00.767 --> 26:04.229
Oh, you're Shin Seo-ri's Supercar,
aren't you? What's Supercar doing here?

26:04.312 --> 26:06.940
-The sup--
-Ah! Ah! Watch where you're going!

26:09.401 --> 26:12.320
So you're not Supercar, you're Shin
Seo-ri's manager? And you're just broke,

26:12.404 --> 26:19.327
not vintage? What are you trying to pull?
You should've said who you are.

26:21.454 --> 26:24.291
Yeah, but I tried to tell you.
You told me not to speak.

26:26.126 --> 26:29.796
Oh! Everything involving Shin Seo-ri is a
disaster.

26:30.338 --> 26:33.383
My job was to drive you here, so
I'm gonna go now.

26:35.927 --> 26:36.761
Oh, wait.

26:36.845 --> 26:39.097
Yes, Ji-hyo. If there's anything else
I can do…

26:39.180 --> 26:41.182
You're won't leave hate comments, right?

26:42.058 --> 26:43.059
Hate comments?

26:43.977 --> 26:47.981
You see, I've been in this business for
20 years, and I've met a lot of assholes

26:48.064 --> 26:53.820
who are nice to your face and then
curse you out behind your back.

26:56.906 --> 26:57.991
So let's not do that.

27:00.076 --> 27:00.910
Yeah?

27:01.536 --> 27:02.370
Got it.

27:04.623 --> 27:05.457
Shit!

27:08.376 --> 27:09.336
I'm not an asshole.

27:12.255 --> 27:16.009
Cha Se-gye. From my window, I can see a
sliver of Namsan Tower, the size of

27:16.092 --> 27:21.306
a fingernail. I was completely unaware it
was so big. I'm so glad we came.

27:23.308 --> 27:27.312
Well, that makes sense, I guess. From my
place, you can see a forearm's length.

27:27.812 --> 27:33.318
A forearm? You have that clear a view?
You've really made it, haven't you?

27:34.861 --> 27:36.738
I've made it because I can see the Tower
clearly?

27:36.821 --> 27:39.324
Of course. I heard that here,
seeing Namsan Tower from your window

27:39.407 --> 27:44.204
is a measure of success. The bigger
you see it, the more success.

27:45.538 --> 27:49.334
Shall we go to my place then? To see how
big the Tower is?

27:53.672 --> 27:55.256
It's even better at night.

27:55.340 --> 27:57.926
I've noticed you're always trying
to get me to go inside a home.

27:58.009 --> 28:00.679
Yesterday, you tried to worm your way
into mine, now you want me to go

28:00.762 --> 28:01.888
to yours?

28:01.971 --> 28:05.642
Wait, my motives were entirely pure.
I just wanted you to see where I live.

28:05.725 --> 28:07.602
Then why does it have to be at night?

28:12.982 --> 28:14.484
Fine. It's because I'm lonely.

28:15.318 --> 28:16.152
You're lonely?

28:16.236 --> 28:18.571
Of course I am. I am not immune to
loneliness.

28:24.911 --> 28:27.914
Mr. Cha must feel so isolated. His family
is awful. I think they were his aunts

28:27.997 --> 28:30.875
and they came to see me earlier today.
I think they were trying to find out

28:30.959 --> 28:33.753
what's going on between the two of you.
Talking about "the door handle to

28:33.837 --> 28:37.549
power" or something like that.

28:41.886 --> 28:45.765
I'm telling you to attach yourself to
him very firmly, like a stick of taffy.

28:48.017 --> 28:53.732
Poverty in the midst of plenty, relative
deprivation. That kind of thing.

28:55.817 --> 28:59.362
This man is opening up to me. Probably
only to me.

28:59.863 --> 29:03.450
Do not worry. I won't let you be lonely,
Cha Se-Gye.

29:04.743 --> 29:05.577
You won't?

29:06.494 --> 29:11.666
I will not let you be alone. You can
trust me.

29:28.808 --> 29:33.605
I will not let you be alone. You can
trust me.

29:35.356 --> 29:41.404
It's a promise, Shin Seo-ri. And it's
too late. Too late to back out.

29:54.834 --> 29:56.544
-Here.
-Oh, thank you.

29:57.587 --> 29:59.255
-For you.
-Thank you so much.

30:00.256 --> 30:01.090
Shin Seo-ri!

30:01.716 --> 30:02.550
Huh?

30:02.634 --> 30:05.053
Why are you in such a good mood? What's
going on?

30:05.136 --> 30:06.638
I'm glad you're here. For you.

30:07.305 --> 30:09.432
Oh, wow. What is it?

30:09.516 --> 30:11.976
Candied apples. I stayed up all night
making them.

30:12.060 --> 30:15.313
Oh, you're even giving gifts. Your life
must be sweet these days.

30:15.396 --> 30:16.439
You enjoy them.

30:17.357 --> 30:20.443
Oh. Look here. Where is the overseer?

30:20.527 --> 30:22.362
The director's on his way. Why?

30:22.445 --> 30:25.448
Share these with him. Here. Don't hog
them all yourself.

30:25.532 --> 30:26.658
Here's your costume.

30:30.245 --> 30:31.871
What's this? A bribe?

30:36.501 --> 30:37.335
Here you go.

30:37.836 --> 30:42.048
Even the bribes she gives are tacky, just
like her. What's with this yakgwa?

30:42.131 --> 30:44.133
They're not yakgwa. They're candied
apples.

30:44.217 --> 30:46.678
I'm not gonna eat this. Who knows
what's in it?

30:53.059 --> 30:58.398
Fucking bastard pricks, god damn
motherfucking wack ass bitches!

31:02.110 --> 31:06.990
What if he writes something nasty?
I should've spoken more firmly with him.

31:14.581 --> 31:18.293
Hey, Shin Seo-ri. I don't like your
manager. You should really fire him.

31:18.376 --> 31:20.003
What sort of nonsense is that?

31:20.545 --> 31:22.422
You've never even met Baek Gwang-nam.

31:23.339 --> 31:26.050
Well, I've seen him around. I got a
shifty vibe from him. Stop arguing.

31:26.134 --> 31:30.638
I'll send you someone suitable, so
just replace him, alright?

31:30.722 --> 31:33.516
Worry about how your own face comes
across, you vixen.

31:34.517 --> 31:35.560
How dare she…

31:36.853 --> 31:39.731
The Chail Songjin Resort construction
still has a long way to go. Why would

31:39.814 --> 31:41.399
he transfer you out of nowhere?

31:41.482 --> 31:44.485
Our retail tenants are also complaining.
They all signed on because of you, Mr.

31:44.569 --> 31:47.906
Choi, they're worried this will slow
things down.

31:47.989 --> 31:51.075
What's the chairman thinking, making a
decision such as this?

31:53.494 --> 31:56.831
He can't be thinking of putting
him in your place, surely? You all

31:56.915 --> 32:00.668
remember when he fired all the CEO's
in HQ and every affiliate, claiming he

32:00.752 --> 32:06.341
was cleaning up mismanagement. It was a
total bloodbath.

32:06.424 --> 32:10.261
How could we forget? I don't care if he's
the chairman's grandson. We can't let

32:10.345 --> 32:13.348
that jerk even set foot in the lobby
of Chail headquarters.

32:16.601 --> 32:19.062
What made you suddenly change your
mind? I thought you wanted to

32:19.145 --> 32:20.104
wait and see.

32:20.188 --> 32:23.149
Well, the best defense is a good offense.
And the best offense is a preemptive

32:23.232 --> 32:24.108
strike.

32:25.652 --> 32:26.736
I can't believe it.

32:30.782 --> 32:32.909
My ears are itching. They must be talking
about me.

32:32.992 --> 32:35.119
So sir, how's it feel to be back again?

32:38.539 --> 32:43.211
The air feels stale. Let's start
by replacing filters.

32:45.171 --> 32:48.549
Calm down, everyone. I'm not going
anywhere. And I won't back down that

32:48.633 --> 32:49.717
easily.

32:59.644 --> 33:03.231
Mr. Choi, Mr. Park, Mr. Jung, it's been
a while. You're all looking much

33:03.314 --> 33:06.317
better than when I last saw you.

33:10.780 --> 33:12.365
Mr. Cha has just entered HQ.

33:12.991 --> 33:16.661
You see, fishing is all about the art of
patience. When the time is right, the

33:16.744 --> 33:18.496
float rises.

33:22.959 --> 33:26.421
What brings you here, Cha? I've heard
some news about you through the

33:26.504 --> 33:29.966
grapevine. I was told you're making
chump change at your little cosmetics

33:30.049 --> 33:31.259
startup.

33:32.760 --> 33:35.805
Actually, I heard you're making
pretty good money by snatching up

33:35.888 --> 33:39.600
the best SME's and flipping them. Even at
Chail, you treated our executives like

33:39.684 --> 33:42.103
cogs in the machine, so I guess nothing's
changed.

33:42.186 --> 33:45.940
While we're on the topic, you know
what the trend is these days? Merit over

33:46.024 --> 33:49.610
bloodline. Blind nepotism is an
outdated notion our business world must

33:49.694 --> 33:51.320
leave behind.

33:54.198 --> 33:57.869
Come on, that's enough The chairman
has always had a soft spot for Se-gye

33:57.952 --> 34:01.622
because of the late Jin-woo. You all
know that. I'm sure there's a reason

34:01.706 --> 34:05.334
our Se-gye has graced us with his
presence here today right? Even though

34:05.418 --> 34:10.798
he hasn't been formally appointed
yet. Isn't that right, Se-gye?

34:15.303 --> 34:19.140
Are you all done talking now? What's the
conclusion then? That I should know

34:19.223 --> 34:22.935
my place and stay away from here? Too
bad. I'm a hothead, and the more you

34:23.019 --> 34:26.439
trample on me, the more competitive
I get. You, Mr. Choi, our CEO of

34:26.522 --> 34:30.401
Distribution. You call startups chump
change? Try making money before running

34:30.485 --> 34:35.907
your mouth. I saw that sales fell 31
percent this quarter, didn't they?

34:36.657 --> 34:38.701
Th-the price of the stock has now
stabilized.

34:38.785 --> 34:41.454
Up next, Mr. Park, CEO of Chail Bio.
You remarked I treated executives

34:41.537 --> 34:44.415
like cogs, yet you punish employees for
taking parental leave, forcing them

34:44.499 --> 34:47.126
into contract work, am I correct?
That's your idea of "human-centered

34:47.210 --> 34:48.711
management?"

34:50.463 --> 34:53.925
Now, Mr. Jung Bon-gu, my eldest aunt's
ex-husband's youngest sister's

34:54.008 --> 34:56.803
cousin, and CEO of Chail Chemicals,
you're next up.

34:57.303 --> 35:00.056
I saw with my own eyes how you
campaigned for a position before you got

35:00.139 --> 35:02.934
divorced, and now you're complaining
about blood relations? You hypocricy

35:03.017 --> 35:05.603
is amazing, considering you're the
greatest profitter of marriage of

35:05.686 --> 35:06.938
convenience.

35:07.438 --> 35:09.190
What? Hy-hy-hy- hypocrisy?

35:09.690 --> 35:13.402
Se-gye, stop this. You haven't been
appointed yet, so you have no right to

35:13.486 --> 35:16.906
barge into a board meeting, even if you
are the chariman's grandson.

35:16.989 --> 35:21.577
Please leave now, we have pressing
matters.

35:24.664 --> 35:27.917
Oh, really? If that's the case,
then shouldn't you be leaving first?

35:28.000 --> 35:31.629
It doesn't make sense for you to
lead this meeting, since you will be

35:31.712 --> 35:35.550
exiled to the U.S. any day now.

35:39.345 --> 35:42.974
I'll make it perfectly clear on my
first official day at Chail. Just how I

35:43.057 --> 35:48.146
managed to get the position regardless of
the half-blood chaebol stigma.

36:00.408 --> 36:03.995
How amusing. Has being on your own,
cosplaying middle class, helped you

36:04.078 --> 36:07.832
gain perspective? Let me guess…

36:10.376 --> 36:12.753
it turns out reality's not so glamourous
is it?

36:13.379 --> 36:15.840
You can stop now with your fake
confidence act. I can tell you're

36:15.923 --> 36:17.717
shitting yourself.

36:17.800 --> 36:20.761
No, you're the one who's been acting.
I've never had the luxury of resting on

36:20.845 --> 36:23.556
my laurels. You and I are fundamentally
different. You were born with a

36:23.639 --> 36:30.563
silver spoon in your mouth, and I had
to work my ass off just to have a chance.

36:31.105 --> 36:34.108
So you're a self-made legend then,
is that what you're saying? Isn't it

36:34.192 --> 36:36.986
thanks to your family connections
that you're even here right now?

36:37.069 --> 36:40.114
Although, I guess this is the last
time that will be the case.

36:40.198 --> 36:43.326
Really? Do you think I'll back down
without a fight?

36:47.371 --> 36:50.791
You should gain some perspective.
There's a limit to how much I'll let

36:50.875 --> 36:54.921
you get away with. I wouldn't have let
things slide for so long.

36:55.463 --> 36:57.215
-What?
-I kept quiet about everything that

36:57.298 --> 37:00.635
you've ever done to me because I
felt a shred of gratitude for you saving

37:00.718 --> 37:02.386
grandfather's life. But,

37:02.929 --> 37:06.390
it's over now, you understand? I won't
tolerate you messing with my people

37:06.474 --> 37:09.852
any longer so quit sneaking around and
come at me with all you got.

37:13.648 --> 37:14.482
Tell me then…

37:16.525 --> 37:17.360
You wanna go?

37:19.862 --> 37:21.322
Oh, anytime.

37:22.615 --> 37:24.492
Ex-CEO Choi Mun-do.

37:40.132 --> 37:43.970
Noona. Why do you need me so urgently?
What's going on?

37:44.470 --> 37:46.138
What happened between you and the vixen?

37:46.222 --> 37:48.474
Uh, nothing. Uh, nothing happened.
Why do you ask?

37:48.557 --> 37:52.353
Really? Then why is she telling me
to fire you?

37:54.313 --> 37:55.398
She told you to fire me?

37:55.481 --> 37:58.317
She was talking nonsense about how
you looked shifty, so I told her

37:58.401 --> 38:01.404
to shut up. But you should be careful.
My influence isn't as strong as hers, so

38:01.487 --> 38:02.321
be cautious.

38:03.656 --> 38:07.034
-And keep your head down.
-Who fires someone because of that?

38:07.118 --> 38:08.119
Okay, I hear ya.

38:13.082 --> 38:15.001
Huh? Your costume…

38:17.670 --> 38:18.587
Oh, my God.

38:31.434 --> 38:34.478
You should've taken better care of your
costume. Wardrobe says they don't have a

38:34.562 --> 38:35.396
backup.

38:35.479 --> 38:39.191
Sorry, but why are you blaming the
actress? Someone obviously sabotaged her.

38:39.275 --> 38:40.359
I'm just frustrated, that's all.
Ugh, this has thrown off the

38:40.443 --> 38:43.154
entire filming schedule. Uh, okay,
we'll shoot the bedroom scene first.

38:43.237 --> 38:44.155
Get the set ready!

38:46.782 --> 38:49.618
All right, come on, get changed. Go get
your hair fixed. Come on, move it,

38:49.702 --> 38:50.703
move it.

38:54.790 --> 38:58.294
Shin Seo-ri's always causing problems.
She really has a way of messing

38:58.377 --> 38:59.754
up the set.

39:00.379 --> 39:01.339
Have you heard the rumors?

39:01.422 --> 39:03.174
Is it time? They're getting the
bullets ready.

39:03.257 --> 39:06.135
Biojei's about to rerate. Let's hit
that hockey stick.

39:06.218 --> 39:10.139
They're like surveillance cameras. How on
earth did they know I was in the HQ

39:10.222 --> 39:11.349
building?

39:12.016 --> 39:13.893
Mr. Cha, how did the preemptive
strike go?

39:13.976 --> 39:16.187
Basically, it was a near-death
experience.

39:16.270 --> 39:18.898
There's a long way to go yet, so let's
take it easy.

39:18.981 --> 39:21.359
You're right. Let's go back to the
office. That was enough of a warm-up,

39:21.442 --> 39:22.276
I think.

39:22.902 --> 39:26.280
First, we need to go to Hannam-dong.
The chairman wants to see you.

39:27.740 --> 39:30.409
Thank you for inviting us, Mr. Cha.
I've heard that you've been taking

39:30.493 --> 39:33.454
good care of my Tae-hee.

39:33.996 --> 39:36.916
I have you to thank for raising such
an intelligent and positive young lady.

39:36.999 --> 39:41.420
My deepest gratitude, I will take
good care of her.

39:41.504 --> 39:43.631
I should be taking good care of you.

39:43.714 --> 39:46.175
She sounds like she's already joined
your family.

39:52.723 --> 39:53.849
Se-gye, hello.

39:57.186 --> 39:58.646
I didn't know you had company.

39:58.729 --> 40:00.106
Yes, come take a seat.

40:07.071 --> 40:10.741
So, what kind of timeframe are you
looking at for the wedding? Tae-hee is

40:10.825 --> 40:14.412
still young and focused on her career, so
I'd really prefer they take their

40:14.495 --> 40:17.540
time and continue dating for a while.

40:18.040 --> 40:21.335
I respect your wishes. We can
proceed with the engagment for now.

40:21.419 --> 40:26.590
I don't mind if the wedding comes later.
You agree, right?

40:30.177 --> 40:34.098
I hope you've enjoyed your lunch today.
If I had known, I would've treated you

40:34.181 --> 40:37.643
to a proper lunch at a restaurant.
This feels far too casual a way to

40:37.726 --> 40:39.770
treat a business partner.

40:44.483 --> 40:47.862
I should be going now, I need to get back
to the office.

40:47.945 --> 40:49.155
Sit down, Se-gye.

40:49.238 --> 40:52.992
If you have something to discuss with me,
I'll come back another time.

40:57.955 --> 41:00.040
I apologize for this disrespect.

41:00.541 --> 41:02.334
I'll see him out, don't worry.

41:02.835 --> 41:06.672
Se-gye, it's disrespectful to walk out
on my mother, you can't just do that.

41:10.050 --> 41:12.386
It would've been avoided if you hadn't
come here today.

41:12.470 --> 41:15.222
Is this because of her? Is that
why you're so rude?

41:16.474 --> 41:19.268
I thought you were smarter, but I see you
have an awful memory. I made it

41:19.351 --> 41:22.229
perfectly clear that I'd go through our
offices to call off the engagement.

41:22.313 --> 41:25.524
Aren't you being disrespectful
by trampling over that agreement?

41:25.608 --> 41:28.235
You know we can't just break it off
overnight. Mochang and Chail

41:28.319 --> 41:32.615
have already signed an MOU, and there
are many things at stake.

41:32.698 --> 41:36.702
That's why I've been turning a blind eye
to your constant disrespect. I don't

41:36.785 --> 41:40.206
ever want to hear you talk about my
woman again. I already feel like

41:40.289 --> 41:43.876
I'm hurting her by being here.

41:52.301 --> 41:55.638
This is so unlike you, why did you
do this? And what made you cook

41:55.721 --> 41:56.555
so many, huh?

41:57.056 --> 41:58.724
It's fine. I'll eat them all myself.

41:58.807 --> 42:02.061
Noona, that's impossible. Just leave
them, I'll take care of it.

42:02.144 --> 42:03.354
What are you going to do?

42:03.437 --> 42:06.607
I'll go to my old school and hand them
out to the students there.

42:06.690 --> 42:11.237
Yeah? That's a good idea. Go now
before they go bad.

42:15.824 --> 42:17.076
Where are you going now?

42:17.159 --> 42:17.993
It's a secret.

42:18.077 --> 42:20.913
What secret? I thought we weren't
going to keep secrets from each other.

42:20.996 --> 42:23.499
I made something, so I came to
see grandma. I'm at the hospital to

42:23.582 --> 42:26.085
-share it with some of the people here.
-Oh, yeah?

42:27.628 --> 42:28.712
Sh-should I join you?

42:29.255 --> 42:32.299
Don't be ridiculous. I've got to go now.

42:36.011 --> 42:39.848
Is it just me? She hasn't treated me
any better since we've become a couple.

42:41.767 --> 42:45.354
It's more concern than affection, if
you ask me. About your well being.

42:45.437 --> 42:49.858
Especially your… stamina. I think
that's what she's concerned about.

42:52.695 --> 42:54.113
I've gotten too soft lately.

42:56.365 --> 42:57.992
It's time I showed my manliness,

42:59.952 --> 43:00.786
Mr. Son.

43:03.455 --> 43:04.873
Wow, thanks, how thoughtful!

43:06.041 --> 43:09.044
I was just thinking that I needed a
pick-me-up. Thank you.

43:09.128 --> 43:11.046
Oh, are these candied apples?

43:11.130 --> 43:14.008
I'm so glad you like it. It's nothing
special. It will make you thirsty, so

43:14.091 --> 43:19.430
get an iced coffee to go with it.
Here you go.

43:19.513 --> 43:21.348
Oh, we'd get into trouble for taking
this.

43:21.432 --> 43:23.684
Really? I'll go and get them myself then.

43:24.184 --> 43:27.646
Hey, you seen the patient in 12?
She's been gone for a while.

43:27.730 --> 43:29.940
Room 12? That's Ms. Nam Ok-sun.

43:33.319 --> 43:36.905
Please give us a moment while we
check the CCTV footage.

43:56.842 --> 43:58.052
SONGJIN GENERAL HOSPITAL

44:17.571 --> 44:20.949
Where on earth has she gone? It'll start
getting dark soon.

44:24.370 --> 44:25.204
Grandma!

44:25.704 --> 44:28.123
-Oh, S- Seo…
-Where were you?

44:29.958 --> 44:32.461
I went… to get some fresh air.

44:32.544 --> 44:35.631
You should've told them you were leaving.
You scared me.

44:36.215 --> 44:39.551
Gosh, why would that scare you, huh?
What am I, a child?

44:42.179 --> 44:44.640
From now on, if you're going outside,
tell someone. And don't go

44:44.723 --> 44:46.225
walking around alone, okay?

44:46.308 --> 44:48.477
Jeez, this is like a prison then.

44:49.019 --> 44:50.813
I can't even do what I want.

44:52.981 --> 44:53.816
What's that?

44:53.899 --> 44:57.820
Huh? Oh, it's nothing. It's nothing. It's
nothing. Don't worry, okay? Oh, hey.

44:57.903 --> 45:01.115
Gosh, I said it's nothing.

45:11.750 --> 45:13.293
LAND SALE AGREEMENT

45:17.047 --> 45:17.923
SELLER
NAM OK-SUN

45:18.006 --> 45:19.425
BUYER: CHAIL E&amp;C
CHOI MUN-DO

45:26.807 --> 45:28.183
It wasn't just a walk then.

45:31.895 --> 45:35.399
To be honest, her mind has been
coming and going a lot lately. I mean,

45:35.482 --> 45:40.529
given her age, it's unlikely to
expect much improvement.

45:51.415 --> 45:52.583
Will you be paying in full?

45:52.666 --> 45:55.461
Of course. Real men always do.

45:55.961 --> 45:57.004
What?

46:00.090 --> 46:03.510
I'm saying you can just charge everything
to that card. It doesn't have a

46:03.594 --> 46:05.512
spending limit, you see. No limit.

46:06.138 --> 46:07.389
Ah, I see.

46:09.600 --> 46:12.728
I've paid like a man should, so
now what's the room number for

46:12.811 --> 46:14.188
Nam Ok-sun?

46:32.581 --> 46:36.376
Ah, let me guess… You're my Seo-ri's
boyfriend?

46:36.877 --> 46:40.339
Yes, ma'am. We're officially dating each
other.

46:43.008 --> 46:44.760
Your features…

46:52.768 --> 46:56.230
are very nice. And manly too.

46:57.231 --> 47:00.275
Right? Yeah, I've been told that many
times.

47:03.278 --> 47:04.738
Uh, yes, thank you.

47:06.365 --> 47:11.161
This may be presumptuous of me, uh,
but could I please ask you a favor?

47:11.245 --> 47:12.663
Yes, ma'am, of course.

47:15.791 --> 47:17.501
When my Seo-ri was growing up…

47:20.420 --> 47:23.882
I barely did anything at all for her.

47:26.802 --> 47:29.263
I was so busy running my restaurant…

47:34.810 --> 47:38.438
she practically raised herself. So when
people said that she was mature,

47:38.522 --> 47:44.611
she took it as a compliment. She liked
hearing people say that to her.

47:47.197 --> 47:53.245
How foolish. A child should be a child.
A child mature for their age

47:53.829 --> 47:54.830
is carrying pain.

47:55.622 --> 48:02.504
So she may be a grown up, but inside of
her, she's a little girl.

48:05.007 --> 48:07.259
I'm afraid she never developed a way…

48:09.803 --> 48:15.142
to look within. I don't care about
anything else. Just don't abandon her.

48:17.185 --> 48:21.982
Please be there for her so she…
doesn't carry that burden alone.

48:24.234 --> 48:25.903
That's all I really want for her.

48:27.863 --> 48:31.241
Yes, ma'am. I won't leave her alone.

48:33.452 --> 48:35.245
I will never let her be lonely.

48:38.624 --> 48:42.753
Then I'm happy. That is musc to my ears.
Yes.

48:49.134 --> 48:52.512
Please don't worry too much, ma'am.
I've done very well for myself,

48:52.596 --> 48:55.599
so she won't ever have to lift a finger.

48:56.266 --> 48:57.935
Boys sure know how to sweet-talk.

49:00.020 --> 49:03.941
I've got a way with words. I have been
told I like to run my mouth.

49:04.942 --> 49:08.070
Oh, goodness. I can't believe I
haven't even offered such an important

49:08.153 --> 49:10.447
guest a glass of water. You wait
right there.

49:10.530 --> 49:11.531
Gosh.

49:36.431 --> 49:40.310
Her granddaughter got so worried when
she suddenly disappeared earlier.

49:40.394 --> 49:42.646
Tell me when. You wanna go?

49:45.857 --> 49:47.109
That crazy bastard.

50:02.791 --> 50:06.461
I knew you were a vicious monster,
but I didn't realize you could be this

50:06.545 --> 50:09.715
shameless. You lured and threatened
a helpless old woman? Have you

50:09.798 --> 50:11.466
any decency?

50:13.969 --> 50:16.972
Well, well. Ms. Shin, you seem
very angry. But let's get the

50:17.055 --> 50:20.726
facts straight, shall we? There was
no threat. We explained everything in

50:20.809 --> 50:26.606
sufficient detail, and she stamped the
agreement on her own accord.

50:27.357 --> 50:31.528
You took advantage of her confusion.
You pretend that isn't a threat?

50:36.158 --> 50:39.786
Your face has always made me feel sick
to my stomach and now I know why.

50:39.870 --> 50:45.542
You have the tongue of a serpent,
that beguiles and deceives. You are vile.

50:47.127 --> 50:49.004
I have been away too long, haven't I?

50:50.380 --> 50:53.300
So it was you. Kang clan, Dan-sim.

50:55.135 --> 50:56.011
Your Royal Highness.

50:56.094 --> 50:59.639
What brings you to my elder brother's
dwelling? No one has set foot here

50:59.723 --> 51:00.557
in a long time.

51:01.308 --> 51:02.142
Pardon?

51:02.225 --> 51:06.354
This used to be the pavilion of my late
elder brother. When I was a young child,

51:06.438 --> 51:09.649
it was my favorite place.

51:14.112 --> 51:16.239
It also was my younger brother's
favorite.

51:17.866 --> 51:20.285
This is my secret spot. What are you
doing here?

51:21.036 --> 51:24.956
He used to tend to this place. He must've
missed our elder brother. That's the

51:25.040 --> 51:26.416
kind of boy he is.

51:26.500 --> 51:27.334
YEONGHWI CHAMBER

51:28.043 --> 51:31.546
A gentle and kind soul. My younger
brother. He may have shut himself off

51:31.630 --> 51:35.801
from the world wearing that half-mask,
but I know…

51:36.593 --> 51:38.678
he too, had dreams of becoming great.

51:38.762 --> 51:39.805
Dreams, sir?

51:39.888 --> 51:42.808
Yes, that grew but were then buried
under.

51:45.352 --> 51:48.313
I know you were close to him and
must find it uncomfortable

51:48.396 --> 51:52.067
to be with me. I did not dislike my
brother at all. Just as there is only

51:52.150 --> 51:59.074
one sun above us, such is the destiny of
those fated to live as royal-born.

52:01.743 --> 52:05.622
Like Hyeon, I also have dreams. I wish to
be a king that will be truly worthy

52:05.705 --> 52:12.629
of his subjects. Kang clan, Dan-sim,
will you stand among my subjects then?

52:24.099 --> 52:27.727
How laughable that I was fooled by that
contemptible face and cowered in

52:27.811 --> 52:29.396
fear for even a second.

52:32.440 --> 52:34.568
Cowered in fear? Really? You?

52:35.068 --> 52:38.238
I once thought that you might
return to me if I waited. That we

52:38.321 --> 52:41.992
might meet again if you were still
alive. I waited like a hopeful fool, not

52:42.075 --> 52:45.787
realizing I was being used. But
no longer. No more will I be manipulated

52:45.871 --> 52:49.457
by such scheming and threats.

53:01.136 --> 53:05.056
Well, none of it matters. The contract
was stamped, and the restaurant will be

53:05.140 --> 53:09.811
demolished. All you have to do now is
pocket the compensation.

53:14.191 --> 53:18.111
Listen. You have nothing to lose, Ms.
Shin. Oh, and… I wish you and Se-gye all

53:18.195 --> 53:24.451
the best too. I'm truly cheering you
on, so don't take it the wrong way.

53:25.660 --> 53:27.537
You're made for each other, honestly.

53:37.088 --> 53:37.923
Cha Se-gye!

53:39.633 --> 53:41.176
Choi Mun-do, you bastard.

53:41.801 --> 53:44.471
You missed our little chat. You two
aren't on the same page, huh?

53:44.554 --> 53:46.431
Shut your mouth before I rip it open.

53:55.273 --> 53:58.902
This piece of paper? It means nothing.
And it's not even binding by law.

53:58.985 --> 54:02.614
I'll throw you in jail for everything
you've ever done. So stay the hell

54:02.697 --> 54:04.866
out of my way, or else I will kill you.

54:22.759 --> 54:25.887
Why did you come here alone?
You should've told me first.

54:25.971 --> 54:27.639
I didn't plan it. It just happened.

54:27.722 --> 54:31.518
You promised me you'd stay away from him
and tell me if anything came up.

54:31.601 --> 54:34.562
I already told you how it happened.
It wasn't my choice to meet with him.

54:34.646 --> 54:37.649
Things just got complicated and--

54:37.732 --> 54:41.236
I don't want you going anywhere near him
alright? I can't stand it!

54:47.117 --> 54:49.703
Whatever it takes to protect you,
I'll do it, okay?

54:54.833 --> 54:58.336
Excuse me? Who do you think you are
to say that to me? Are you already my

54:58.420 --> 55:02.841
husband or something? Is that why
you treat me like a fool?

55:03.508 --> 55:05.135
I didn't mean it like that.

55:05.218 --> 55:08.430
You're worse than he is. You hurt
me more by treating me like an idiot,

55:08.513 --> 55:10.056
pretending to take care of me!

55:14.561 --> 55:16.646
Don't follow me. I don't want to see you.

55:32.704 --> 55:37.917
I don't care about anything else.
Just don't abandon her.

55:58.188 --> 55:59.856
You've come without notice.

56:05.987 --> 56:06.821
What brings you here?

56:06.905 --> 56:09.783
Sir, I have something important to
tell you about Se-gye.

56:24.714 --> 56:27.342
How's your morning, Mr. Cha. Argh, Jesus
Christ!

56:27.425 --> 56:29.094
I've had better ones.

56:29.177 --> 56:32.097
Your face. Nightmares or something?

56:32.180 --> 56:33.348
My life is a nightmare.

56:34.599 --> 56:35.600
I'm such an idiot.

56:36.101 --> 56:38.144
What have you done this time?

56:38.228 --> 56:41.106
My mouth is the problem. Why did I
say that? I should have just shut up and

56:41.189 --> 56:42.524
comforted her.

56:43.733 --> 56:46.486
What a dumbass. Can't I control my
temper at all?

56:46.986 --> 56:47.987
Well,

56:48.071 --> 56:50.407
that's not the only thing you can't
control.

56:50.990 --> 56:55.120
I can't stand to not see her. This is
no way for me to live.

56:57.914 --> 57:00.458
Ah… I suddenly need caffeine.

57:04.421 --> 57:06.548
A boss's love life is exhausting.

57:08.007 --> 57:08.842
What'd you say?

57:08.925 --> 57:11.511
Oh? Uh, sorry, I'm sorry I'm… uh…
Nothing, nothing.

57:12.178 --> 57:16.099
The… uh, oh, ch-check, check the
center console. Please.

57:18.226 --> 57:20.353
Have some of that to relieve your
fatigue.

57:23.523 --> 57:26.317
-I stocked up especially for you.
-This supposedly helps with that?

57:26.401 --> 57:28.236
Oh, uh, it seems to be very popular.

57:33.533 --> 57:36.369
Man, I feel like my circulation is going
again.

57:41.749 --> 57:43.126
What a selfish prick.

57:43.209 --> 57:46.254
I want a guard positioned at the
grandmother's room. If anyone

57:46.337 --> 57:51.134
suspicious is caught lurking, notify me.
And get out of the car. Right now.

57:54.095 --> 57:54.929
Are you serious?

58:18.328 --> 58:21.998
I did tell him not to follow me, but how
could he just let me go? Must he

58:22.081 --> 58:23.583
be so petty?

58:27.587 --> 58:31.299
Actually. I did say I didn't want to see
him, so I guess he had no choice.

58:31.382 --> 58:38.306
Still, he could text or call. Why is he
tormenting me? Damn that jerk.

58:42.519 --> 58:45.188
You're worse than he is. You hurt me
more by treating me like an idiot,

58:45.271 --> 58:46.773
pretending to take care of me!

58:49.275 --> 58:56.199
Ugh, you idiot. Why did you take
it out on him? He didn't deserve it.

59:06.876 --> 59:11.256
I should eat something. I need my
strength if I'm going to fight and win.

59:31.693 --> 59:35.655
Oh, boy. This place is going to go out of
business any day now. It's completely

59:35.738 --> 59:36.573
empty.

59:37.198 --> 59:40.535
It's break time. I only let you in
because you're a regular. Want to be

59:40.618 --> 59:41.995
kicked out of here? Get out!

59:42.078 --> 59:44.581
My goodness, you still have plenty
of energy. You could run this

59:44.664 --> 59:47.875
-place another ten years.
-You rotten old man. You want a large?

59:50.128 --> 59:52.088
I'm alone. Why would I want a large?

59:52.171 --> 59:53.506
Your friend's right there.

01:00:13.318 --> 01:00:16.154
What kind of asshole drives down
an alleyway like that?

01:00:18.573 --> 01:00:24.078
Oh, Mr. Cha. Are you here to see Seo-ri?
She's out, left a while ago.

01:00:24.621 --> 01:00:25.455
How long ago?

01:00:34.297 --> 01:00:38.051
You know, Se-gye just makes me angry, I
don't know why. He's as stubborn as

01:00:38.134 --> 01:00:41.429
an ox, never listens, and always
wants to do everything on his own.

01:00:41.512 --> 01:00:48.478
When he was little, I used to hit him,
thinking I could win against a kid.

01:00:51.439 --> 01:00:55.026
Looking back, I feel truly bad about it.
I wish I had just embraced and

01:00:55.109 --> 01:00:59.572
nurtured him. I really do regret it.

01:01:02.367 --> 01:01:06.079
He must've been lonely without a mom.
But instead of comforting him, I was

01:01:06.162 --> 01:01:08.373
always riding him.

01:01:29.352 --> 01:01:32.730
That's why I really want him to
have a family of his own, so as not

01:01:32.814 --> 01:01:37.402
to be lonely. That's all I want for him.

01:01:42.281 --> 01:01:44.701
If that's your wish, then you
musn't worry. I know too well how

01:01:44.784 --> 01:01:51.708
wretched it is to be lonely. I won't let
him be alone in this world.

01:01:52.959 --> 01:01:55.586
No, that's not what I mean. I don't
want him to be with a person just

01:01:55.670 --> 01:01:58.005
as lonely as he is.

01:01:59.674 --> 01:02:03.136
I don't want somebody who doesn't
have enough for herself to fill his

01:02:03.219 --> 01:02:06.597
emptiness. I want him to be with
a woman who has enough to give and

01:02:06.681 --> 01:02:09.767
also has plenty left over for her.

01:02:11.561 --> 01:02:15.273
It's not that I dislike you. I'm just…
a selfish old man. I want Se-gye to

01:02:15.356 --> 01:02:19.026
be surrounded by love, a big family,
in-laws who encourage him and who he

01:02:19.110 --> 01:02:24.949
can depend on, that's what I want
for his life.

01:02:30.121 --> 01:02:31.873
Is that too much to ask for?

01:02:43.050 --> 01:02:43.885
There you are.

01:02:45.845 --> 01:02:46.679
Hi, Dad!

01:02:54.479 --> 01:02:55.897
I missed you Seo-Jun.

01:02:55.980 --> 01:02:56.856
I missed you too.

01:03:11.037 --> 01:03:11.871
CHA SE-GYE

01:03:14.415 --> 01:03:16.334
Oh, pick it up. It's okay.

01:03:42.860 --> 01:03:44.195
Boy, I missed you.

01:03:57.667 --> 01:03:59.836
Your call cannot be connected and is
being…

01:04:27.029 --> 01:04:30.616
CHA SE-GYE

01:04:47.758 --> 01:04:50.928
Your call cannot be connected and
is being forwarded to voicemail.

01:04:51.012 --> 01:04:53.097
Please leave your message after the beep.

01:04:55.182 --> 01:04:56.017
Shin Seo-ri,

01:04:56.934 --> 01:04:58.769
MISSED CALL
CHA SE-GYE

01:04:58.853 --> 01:05:00.897
I'm sorry okay? Can you pick up, please?

01:05:00.980 --> 01:05:01.814
I'm sorry.

01:05:01.898 --> 01:05:03.357
I'll wait until you get here.

01:05:28.633 --> 01:05:32.345
MY ROYAL NEMESIS

01:05:53.407 --> 01:05:56.369
NAMSAN DATE

01:06:00.206 --> 01:06:02.541
-Shin Seo-ri.
-You can't come in here. Sir, you can't.

01:06:02.625 --> 01:06:05.002
Get out of my way. Shin Seo-ri, wake up.
Shin Seo-ri, wake up!

01:06:05.086 --> 01:06:06.420
-Coming through.
-Make way, please.

01:06:06.504 --> 01:06:07.338
Quickly, quickly!

01:06:07.421 --> 01:06:10.007
Who'd have thought Choi Mun-do was
capable of this?

01:06:10.841 --> 01:06:13.135
Chairman Choi Mun-do will now give a
speech.

01:06:13.219 --> 01:06:16.097
He is facing public backlash after
carginogenic substances were detected in

01:06:16.180 --> 01:06:17.723
Dynastie products.

01:06:17.807 --> 01:06:20.601
She was found dead under suspicious
circumstances. And items belonging to

01:06:20.685 --> 01:06:22.395
you were found at her home.

01:06:22.478 --> 01:06:24.939
Your Highness, can you hear me?

01:06:25.022 --> 01:06:27.024
-This place is…
-Bring the physician.

01:06:27.108 --> 01:06:28.609
Have I truly returned here?
